  <!-- ============ SECTION 19 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s19"><span class="num">19</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="three-col">
    <div class="card cn">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Kaufmann</div><div class="glossary-def">A merchant under HGB – anyone conducting a commercial trade, or automatically deemed one by legal form (e.g. any Kapitalgesellschaft).</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Sachverständiger Dritter</div><div class="glossary-def">The "expert third party" standard §238 uses to test whether bookkeeping is sufficiently clear and traceable.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card cn">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Inventar</div><div class="glossary-def">The detailed, itemised physical listing of every asset and liability with individual values, distinct from the condensed Bilanz.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Radierverbot</div><div class="glossary-def">The prohibition on altering an entry in a way that destroys the ability to reconstruct the original content.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card cn">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Festwert</div><div class="glossary-def">A fixed value carried unchanged year to year for low-value, regularly-replenished, immaterial asset categories.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Stichprobeninventur</div><div class="glossary-def">Statistical, sample-based stocktaking, extrapolated to the full population using recognised methods.</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>

